- **apps (rdme, examples, accesskit_xplat; `bump` left the workspace with upstream's `23b9b26a9` "Delete the bump crate", merged at 2026-10-17-upstream-sync-engine-debts):** no tests — observed absent · searched: `#\[(tokio::)?test\]` over the 86 files of slice s04 (hits only in the six browser files above); `examples/seven_guis` holds eight integration-test targets (seven until 2026-10-19-session-recording added `tests/recording.rs`), one shared module that is no target, `tests/common/mod.rs` (the state directory, the leftover clear, the kill-and-reap `Host` guard and, since 2026-10-10-driver-cli, the stream drain, one bounded run of the binary as a client — `Ran`, `run`, `client` — the readers of an answer's one line, `keys`, `number` and `cause`, and the `Started` guard that stops a started session; since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface `string_at`, the outer-layer reader of a JSON string, and `Speaker` with `Spoke` — a child spoken to over piped stdin, its stdout read line by line on a thread under the 30 s `REPLY_BOUND`, every reply asserted free of an ESC byte, the child killed and reaped in its `Drop`; since 2026-10-19-test-splits the log checks' fragment, stated once — `Needles` and `stand_needles` (the CRUD stand's id and name needles, asserted non-empty and no part of the sentinel), `stamped_lines` (every stderr line stamped `service.name=seven_guis`), `found`, `occurrences`, the unix-only `recorded_needles` and `cells_needles(part)` (part `part`'s author keys of the in-process Cells screen and the middle column-A cell it holds) — called by `host_log` and `mcp_log` alone (examples/seven_guis/tests/common/mod.rs:371-544), and `option_needles()`, the needle list of a select's options read from a snapshot, called by the same two (examples/seven_guis/tests/common/mod.rs:425-453); read through `mod common;` by all eight) and a script directory that is no target, `tests/flows/`: since 2026-10-07-driver-session `tests/host_binary.rs` (2 tests)
 — the `escher-session` binary in its host role, `serve <task> --session <dir> [--record <dir>]`, serves a counter session, answers under the binary's own pid, stops, exits 0 with nothing on stdout, its stderr stamped `service.name=seven_guis`, and leaves no state directory, and a host that cannot serve ends as a session error, exit 3; nine argv rows that are no command each end as a usage error, exit 2, their usage line holding nothing the caller typed, with nothing booted and no state created — run as `cargo test -p seven_guis --locked --test host_binary`; and since 2026-10-07-sink-target-allowlist `tests/host_log.rs` (5 tests, unix only, the fourth and the open list's below; 1 until 2026-10-19-session-recording added a recording host that logs nothing of its check at `trace`, and the third reading the clients of a recording session — `start crud --record` through `stop`, a part read and a `lint` among them — 0 needles of each class over their own stderr at `trace`, examples/seven_guis/tests/host_log.rs:45-135) — the `escher-session` binary on `crud` at `RUST_LOG=trace` exits 0 with nothing on stdout and no state directory, every stderr line stamped `service.name=seven_guis`, and no stable id and no accessible name on stderr, its needles read from the stand itself, and since 2026-10-10-driver-cli while a hosted `snapshot`, `click` and `type` run on it: three `command` span lines for the three calls, and 0 occurrences of the typed sentinel beside 0 ids and 0 names — run as `cargo test -p seven_guis --locked --test host_log` and, for the host the workspace build makes, as `cargo test --workspace --locked --test host_log`; since 2026-10-10-driver-cli `tests/cli_commands.rs` (15 tests, unix only: every driver command run as a process of the binary — §6 → Drivers per surface; since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot a `screenshot` answering one line whose `png`, decoded by a hand base64 reader and its PNG header, equals the PNG `Session::run` returns in process;
 since 2026-10-12-self-description `help` answering the tool's description and reaching no session, and a state directory of 94 bytes holding a session where one of 95 is refused `state-dir-too-long` with its bound, and, since 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep, on every target but Linux one of 90 bytes holding a session where one of 91 ends `state-dir-too-long`, status 3, its message holding no path — the two through one shared helper that asserts the message holds not the given directory, so the 94 case asserts it too; the file counts 11 on Linux and 11 on macOS, the 90 case measured on the macOS matrix leg, CI#38642493451, job 116123587286 — examples/seven_guis/tests/cli_commands.rs:766-770; since 2026-10-14-quality-gates a run with its stdout closed before it starts keeps its ending's status — `help` 0, `snapshot` with no session 3 with exactly `NoSession`'s message — printing no panic and creating no state directory, examples/seven_guis/tests/cli_commands.rs:696-758), `tests/cli_flow.rs` (2, unix only: the two shell flows of `tests/flows/` under plain `sh`) and `tests/host_timer.rs` (1, unix only: the timer host moved by a hosted `advance`) — run as `cargo test -p seven_guis --locked --test {name}`; since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface `tests/mcp_server.rs` (6 tests: the binary's `mcp` role completes the Counter flow by tool calls alone — `initialize`, `tools/list` offering the verbs in order, twelve, `start`, `snapshot`, `click` — answers a `lint` tool call with its line of findings, and answers a `server/discover`, a non-JSON line, a 65,537-byte line, an unknown tool, a refused and a malformed call each without running anything, the next snapshot equal and no reply holding the refused id, the tool name or the filler; and, unix only, a fresh Counter's `snapshot` reads the same through MCP and through the command line;
 since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot a `screenshot` tool call answered with an image block then a text block (examples/seven_guis/tests/mcp_server.rs:308-338); since 2026-10-12-self-description the newest revision `2025-11-25` spoken — `2026-07-28` answered with it — and `help` answered before any `start`, and, unix only, `help` reading the same bytes through MCP and through the command line) and `tests/mcp_log.rs` (3 tests, the open list's below — 1 until 2026-10-19-session-recording added a recording `mcp` role that logs nothing of its checks at `trace`, unix-gated, reading the shared `common::recorded_needles` (its own until 2026-10-19-test-splits): the role on `crud` at `RUST_LOG=trace` writes 0 typed-sentinel occurrences, 0 id needles and 0 name needles on stderr, one `tool_call` line per call with only its stated field names, and protocol lines only on stdout; since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot it and `host_log` also drive shots and read 0 occurrences of a shot's first 64 base64 characters on stderr, under both builds — examples/seven_guis/tests/host_log.rs:514-527; examples/seven_guis/tests/mcp_log.rs:190-203) — not unix-gated but the CLI comparisons, two since 2026-10-12-self-description (examples/seven_guis/tests/mcp_server.rs:360-380; examples/seven_guis/tests/mcp_server.rs:382-423), so the windows job runs them, run as `cargo test -p seven_guis --locked --test mcp_server --test mcp_log` and, for the workspace build, `cargo test --workspace --locked --test mcp_server --test mcp_log`; since 2026-10-19-session-recording `tests/recording.rs` (4 tests, unix only, and 1 off-unix; 3 until 2026-10-19-recorded-check-replay) — the command line and the `mcp` role keep the same check byte for byte, the state directory gone after `stop`; a recording directory open to its group refused before anything runs; the `mcp` role's listing and `help` the same with and without `--record`;
 since 2026-10-19-recorded-check-replay the committed checks what the binary records, `record_checks.sh` run through the binary and both files compared byte for byte with the committed copies (examples/seven_guis/tests/recording.rs:205-262); off unix, `--record` refused `Unsupported` — run as `cargo test -p seven_guis --locked --test recording` and in the stand-repeat leg; and since 2026-10-07-act-by-id the library's first unit test, `stand::tests::the_timer_step_carries_milliseconds_onto_whole_ticks` — six cumulative rows of milliseconds onto Timer ticks and two carry rows, the remainder below one tick carried across calls — and `stand::tests::the_timer_step_takes_the_largest_advance` (examples/seven_guis/src/stand.rs:331-343), run as `cargo test -p seven_guis --locked --lib stand::`, and since 2026-10-16-fast-failing-mutants its second, `tasks::timer::tests::a_delivered_tick_is_taken_once_and_an_empty_wait_parks`, in a `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` after the Timer's `CSS` constant, polling the private `TimerTicks::next()` under `Waker::noop()` over a three-row table, the row count asserted, `TimerTicks::next` keeping its one caller, `Timer` (examples/seven_guis/src/tasks/timer.rs:197-226) — `cargo test -p seven_guis --locked --lib` reads 3 passed, as measured at escher-0.2.0/chunks/2026-10-18-one-virtual-clock/report.md; since 2026-10-10-driver-cli `host_timer` boots `escher-session` on `timer`, the one task whose session carries a time step, and moves it by a hosted `advance` with no sleep — 250 ms asked reads `advanced_ms` 250 with the elapsed text two ticks on, every ask reporting exactly the `ms` asked (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-18) — and `cli_commands` starts, reads and stops all six served tasks (`counter` · `flight-booker` · `timer` · `crud` · `cells` · `load`); until then that branch of the host was booted by hand only (escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-act-by-id/evidence/timer-host-boot.md);
 the other examples — the root example `multi_doc`, built by `cargo build --workspace` within `fast`'s clippy, among them — and the apps named still hold no tests (examples/seven_guis/tests/host_binary.rs:19-159; examples/seven_guis/tests/host_log.rs:33-608; examples/seven_guis/tests/cli_commands.rs:134-664; examples/seven_guis/tests/cli_commands.rs:665-839; examples/seven_guis/tests/cli_flow.rs:31-88; examples/seven_guis/tests/host_timer.rs:22-126; examples/seven_guis/tests/mcp_server.rs:100-259; examples/seven_guis/tests/mcp_server.rs:261-381; examples/seven_guis/tests/mcp_server.rs:382-423; examples/seven_guis/tests/mcp_log.rs:53-315; examples/seven_guis/tests/common/mod.rs:1-544; examples/seven_guis/src/stand.rs:246-344; the two MCP targets as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-mcp-surface/report.md, the four new tests at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-12-self-description/report.md, the screenshot's two and the image-byte readings at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-12-headless-screenshot/report.md)

- **blitz-dom covered behaviours:** media type defaults, disabled state, id map, redraw-after-mutation, in-document flags, style-property relayout, rule-tree copy-on-write (packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:1581-2028); zoom redraw, hover cursor, hover/checked/pseudo/background-image invalidation, `@font-face` alias registration (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:3527-4100); the hint-less `@font-face` source, its format sniffed from its bytes (upstream #1109), by blitz-tests' `font_face_sniffed_source` 2 since 2026-10-14-quality-gates — offline, every request held by the shared stand-in `fixtures::HeldNet` (§8), a font context holding no family, both layout modes: the `data:` source requested exactly once and a `wOF2` body registered, a body no sniff matches registering nothing, the file installing no subscriber and printing nothing (tests/blitz-tests/tests/font_face_sniffed_source.rs:50-99); the changed set — `has_changes` false on a fresh document and true from a tracked write until `take_changed_nodes` drains it, a write outside the document and a hover marking nothing, a focus move marking both nodes and a checked change its node, an idle `resolve` marking nothing in either layout mode, a drained id of a dropped node reading `None` (packages/blitz-dom/src/document_changed_set_tests.rs:1-235); since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot the font reading — `can_paint_text` true on a context holding a decodable font and false on one holding no family (packages/blitz-dom/src/document_font_reading_tests.rs:1-26) — while `layout_as_text_input`, public since that chunk, has no unit test of its own and is read through the password mask's frames (`password_painted_masked`); `@font-face` style mapping (packages/blitz-dom/src/net.rs:609-649);
 since 2026-10-19-visual-lint the read-only reader `BaseDocument::text_extent` (`TextExtent { content, text }`), by blitz-tests' `text_extent` 6, both layout modes, on HTML pages booted with the stand's options — a line that cannot wrap reads wider than its box, a wrapped paragraph reads inside its box, and an element with no inline content or a stale id made by `remove_and_drop_node` reads `None` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/text_extent.rs:42-118); its own auto-discovered target, run by the workspace `test` leg, the `stand-repeat` leg (a named `--test` of its list), `run text_extent` and `run all`, not by `run stand`;
 its stated limits are asserted by three of those tests under `-p blitz-tests` and `--workspace` — RTL text read as a left-to-right line from the content box, `#rtl` first asserted to carry `dir="rtl"`; vertical text read as a horizontal line, its twin's line first asserted wider than it is high; a transformed box's lines read at its client rect, which is 2 × its own transform-blind `offset_rect` about the same centre, the lines unscaled (tests/blitz-tests/tests/text_extent.rs:127-152; tests/blitz-tests/tests/text_extent.rs:154-174; tests/blitz-tests/tests/text_extent.rs:176-205); the `select` model — its rules by the `node::select` unit tests and, over a Dioxus page in both layout modes, by blitz-tests' `select_interaction` (the box holding the chosen option, the markup seed, the arrows, `Home` and `End`, the typeahead over one second of the document's clock, one `input` and one `change` per changed choice, the disabled gate on key and click, a `selected` write re-seeding the choice) — it models a `multiple` select and an `optgroup`'s options, asserted by `select_interaction` and, through the driver, by `stand_act_select`; a closed single select opens a list the engine paints over the page on a click, Enter or Space, read by blitz-tests' `select_popup` (below) and `select_interaction` (`enter_and_space_open_the_list_and_a_released_space_does_nothing_more`, tests/blitz-tests/tests/select_interaction.rs:358-396); a closed single select's option is refused `covered`, under a group too (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_select.rs:457-466); a `multiple` select's `size` hints a height of `size × 1.2em` through `size_rows`, capped at 65534, `0` or a bad value hinting nothing, read by `select_popup`'s `size_makes_a_multiple_select_that_many_rows_tall_and_a_key_brings_the_next_in` and `node::select_list`'s `size_reads_a_whole_number_above_zero_capped` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/select_popup.rs:995-1032; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/select_list.rs:459-475), while a single select's `size` is unread; a group's label is named in the tree and painted as a header over its options, read by `select_popup`'s `groups_read_as_headers_their_options_under_them_and_a_header_chooses_nothing` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/select_popup.rs:805-855); an option with no author key reading in `unkeyed_actionable` is asserted by no check; a `<label>` naming every labelable element is pinned by `accessibility_label`; a click on a single select's label focuses the select and opens nothing, with no re-dispatch, asserted by `select_popup`'s `a_labels_click_focuses_the_select_and_opens_nothing` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/select_popup.rs:428-441), while a click on a `multiple` select's label re-dispatched to it is asserted by no check;
 hit testing past a node dropped since the last resolve (`Node::hit_inner` and the paint tree), by blitz-tests' `hit_test_dropped_nodes` 1 (tests/blitz-tests/tests/hit_test_dropped_nodes.rs:32-82); the process-wide `PARALLEL_TRAVERSAL_LOCK`, serialising every `StyleThreading::Parallel` traversal, is asserted by no check — no headless document (harness, stand or driver) sets `Parallel`, and the windowed smoke of `seven_guis_native` under `dioxus_native::launch` is its one local reading
